r 1 and 2 , can only be claimed under form \"M\".It is the Authority which can only deal with the matter falling under proviso to section 18(1).\r\n2. The RERA Appellate Tribunal vide judgement dated 27.02.2019, passed in Appeal no-53 of 2019 has specifically stated at page number-44 of the judgement, that the matters arising under the proviso, cannot be placed before the Adjudicating Officer, but shall be placed entirely before the Authority.\r\n3. As regard to relief claimed at point number 3 of the prayer, can only be dealt by the Authority as matter falls under  section 11(4)(f) of the Act and can only be claimed under form \"M\".\r\nAlso no supporting documents have been uploaded.\r\nKindly rectify the defects and re submit your complaint immediately as per regulations.\r\n\r\n',2,0,'amlegalrera','2019-12-16 14:31:39.000','amlegalrera','2019-12-16 14:31:39.000'),(3577,440007,'amlegalrera','2019-12-16 14:33:12.000',1618,'AdCNo14592019','','','Authority Desk','In-Complete Application (Additional Information Sought by the Authority)','7330c9a0-4296-4ddf-a421-0d0c491adf2d','','2019-12-16 01:10:43.949','','2019-12-16 01:10:43.949','','1. It has been observed that the relief\'s so claimed at point number 1 and 2 falls within the proviso to section 18(1). Since the allottee does not wish to withdraw from the project, hence the following above said prayers at point number 1 and 2 , can only be claimed under form \"M\".It is the Authority which can only deal with the matter falling under proviso to section 18(1).\r\n2. The RERA Appellate Tribunal vide judgement dated 27.02.2019, passed in Appeal no-53 of 2019 has specifically stated at page number-44 of the judgement, that the matters arising under the proviso, cannot be placed before the Adjudicating Officer, but shall be placed entirely before the Authority.\r\n3. As regard to relief claimed at point number 3 of the prayer, can only be dealt by the Authority as matter falls under  section 11(4)(f) of the Act and can o